14.0.4
- Added Form Fillable Character Sheet (PDF-style layout) as the default for new PCs.
- Classic sheet remains available and is forced for VsD monster/NPC imports.
- Click skill, lore, weapon, save, or stat names on the form sheet to roll via the existing modifier dialog.

14.0.3
- Dragging Kin/Vocation Containers onto a PC sheet now auto-deploys packed Modifiers/Traits (ActorSheetV2 drop return shape fixed).
- Sheet form controls use paper background + ink text (fixes black-on-black inputs under Theme V2).

14.0.2
- Aged-paper monochrome UI theme for sheets, chat, combat rows, and dialogs.

14.0.1
- Fixed actor create crash: BaseActor.prepareBaseData now calls super (V14 Active Effect phase init).
- Softened preCreateActor updateSource payload (no longer wipes system data).
- ContextMenu uses HTMLElement instead of jQuery.
- Token/Combat/Actor classes use Foundry V13+ namespaces (removes Token global deprecation).
- Item sheets: fix options.parts (use _configureRenderParts, not object assignment).
- renderTemplate → foundry.applications.handlebars.renderTemplate.
- Personal-use content: added missing Core Rules bestiary (Boggart, Boggle, Demon, Dragonspawn, Fomorian, Ghost, Merlock, Spirit, Undead Thralls, Wraith); Halfling Superstitious kin trait; pack tooling under tools/.

14.0.0
- Foundry V14 compliance pass (system id remains `vsd`).
- Fixed pack paths for vsd-macros and vsd-items (LevelDB folders, not missing `.db` files).
- Replaced removed Token#toggleEffect with ActiveEffect / Actor#toggleStatusEffect (img/name).
- Migrated chat hook from renderChatMessage to renderChatMessageHTML.
- Removed template.json from the shipped system (documentTypes + TypeDataModels only).
- Manifest URLs point at khaleb7/vsdfoundryvibe GitHub Release assets.
- Compatibility: minimum 13, verified 14.

13.0.0
- Community Foundry V13/V14 port (system id remains `vsd`).
- Migrated Actor/Item sheets to ApplicationV2 (HandlebarsApplicationMixin + ActorSheetV2/ItemSheetV2).
- Replaced template.json with documentTypes + TypeDataModels in module/data/models.js.
- Combat tracker updated for ApplicationV2 PARTS; VsD action declaration UI retained.
- Scene control button registration updated for V13 object-shaped controls.
- Status effect / token HUD helpers use name+img (V14-safe); removed TokenDocument.effects/overlayEffect usage.
- CSS wrapped in @layer vsd with Theme V2 scaffolding in test.css.
- Manifest compatibility: minimum 13, verified 13, maximum removed.

12.290
- swapped out the Magic Points item in the VsD Actor Items compendium for one 
with a new formula `((@level.voc+@level.stat) * @level.ranks) + @kinmp` for the 
max value.
- updated all of the vocation Container items in the VsD Items compendium to 
include their Magic Stat and applicable Spell Lores.
- The max Magic Points are now calculated automatically if you use any of the 
mechanisms available in the Kin: Modifier items to modify KinMP, or in the 
Vocation: Variable items to set the MP per Level and/or the Magic Stat.

12.289
- added a rudimentary ERA xml importer to the scripts tab. Paste the contents 
of an ERA XML file into the text area, click outside it, then click on the 
importer text. Wait until the text area clears.
- added the plain text notes field back onto the sheet below the rich text 
notes field.
- bugfix: removed the call to core content actor items as there are none.

12.288
- fixed a bunch of html mistakes that creep in with auto-formatting that caused 
behaviour errors. Collapsing sections should collapse again and skill totals 
should provide a proper accounting again.

12.287
- added an initiative setting for the Foundry default combat tracker of 
`CONFIG.Combat.initiative.formula = "@bs.value"` which will draw the initiative 
value from the sheet whenever you roll, or reroll initiative in the combat 
tracker. It will not do it automatically when you advance the round; you would 
have to reset initiative, run a macro to roll the initiative for selected 
tokens, and then roll all in the tracker to update them with a new initiative 
value. There are many other options available to you if you alter the CONFIG 
setting above, because you may access any data values inside the actor.system 
object from that formula if you know what you are doing, or just change it to 
"2d10" if you like. Have fun!

12.286
- updated the token-tooltip-alt-vsd-config.json to work on v12. It is located 
in data/systems/vsd/data-toolbox/data/
- the sling attacks now properly indicate whether they are for the 1st round or 
the 2nd round of prep.
- the grapple,kick and punch weapon containers now contain all five sized 
attacks with the max value preset and appropriately named. Actor templates and 
default actor items have been updated to contain the medium attack size by 
default.
- it was noted that while checking the perm setting for a modifier changed the 
colour to bright green, unchecking it did not revert the colour to dull green. 
This is because the colour indicates whether or not the modifier is inEffect 
and while checking perm toggles it to true, unchecking it does not toggle it to 
false. There was a reason a very long time ago for making it behave like that 
but I cannot remember what it was. :-)

12.285
- updated the template actors to make them a bit easier to use.

12.284
- The Macro Update
- the code under the macros folder has been cleaned up and the compendium items 
have been updated.
- Folder Items (Copy, Delete and Update) - now permit all world actors to be 
affected at once.
- Folder Join Journals - combines all journals in a folder into a single 
journal.
- Folder PrototypeToken Config - allows you to create and change the Token 
settings for all actors in a folder.
- Token Compendium Items Copy - copies all the items from a named world 
compendium onto the selected tokens.
- Token Items Delete - is very dangerous and allows you to set some criteria to 
select the items that will be deleted from the selected tokens.
- Unlock Compendia - maybe not useful to most but it unlocks all compendia at 
once. You could easily write a reverser to lock all compendia as well.
- VsD Health Adjustment - allows you to generate draggable Damage, Healing and 
Soul Damage in a chat message.
- VsD Declare Selected Token Actions - allows you to select tokens and make 
their action declarations. Very useful for the GM.
- VsD Get Target Defences - generates draggable EDB data in a chat message. 
Drag the value onto the attacker to set their EDB. Haven't used this one in a 
while because there is better support in the attack dialog now.
- VsD Set Combat Tracker Actions - allows you to reconfigure the actions that 
one can declare in combat. Useful if you want to modify the phased declaration 
system. It needs to be run after each world refresh, however.
- VsD Toggle Shield Position - allows you to do this for the selected token.
- VsD Set Movement Rate - changes the Move Rate item value for the selected 
tokens.
- VsD Set Weapon Length - places a light fan in the front arc of the token at 
the length you choose. The is a house rule that may or may not be useful to 
you.
- VsD Vision Light Settings - this is an old one refreshed for v12 and uses 
the vision trait on the selected tokens to determine their actual vision range 
and quality based on the lighting conditions where they are. It also allows you 
to plant a light source on them at the same time. It will not take the light 
source into account for the vision range so you may need to set them both at 
the same time.

12.283
- added a vsd-status-effects compendium to work with the status effects panel
- added effects for Charging, Flank Attack, Rear Attack and Full & Half Action
- removed the condition items from all compendium actors as they are now 
redundant

12.282
- removed about 2200 lines of old and unused data from each stored actor. Not a 
huge saving, but it was annoying to filter through when trying to edit actors 
manually.
- cleaned up any remaining modifiers or variables with a blank first entry. 
There were a couple of hundred of them and they are confusing to people just 
starting to use the system and who missed the transition.
- added a compendium folder to group the base system compendiums and make the 
compendium sidebar a bit tidier.

12.281
- made a style adjustment that affects the core-content module by removing the 
default shadows behind folder header text. It makes folders with light or 
bright backgrounds less readable in the base system, however, so darken or dim 
them a bit to compensate.
- updated the code in the migration script to avoid deprecation messages for 
when I next need to use it.
- tuned the containers a bit so it is obvious that you may now use the notes 
field for notes and so the deploy and remove items buttons are below the group 
field.

12.280
- changed the field name for targets in Modifiers to "Target1, Target2, ..." 
to help people use them as intended.
- changed the behaviour of Container items so they do not automatically drop 
their items when added to an actor but show the Container sheet as with other 
items. They still remove their items when deleted though. A couple of 
"buttons" have been added to the Container sheet, so that you may deploy and 
remove their items from their actor. Be careful not to deploy them more than 
once or you will orphan previously dropped items; although that is a sneaky 
way to permanently add some items to your actor before removing the Container.
- you may now add Containers to other Containers. Be careful with this feature.
- added a per-client setting to delay the refresh of dialog windows so the 
update of data has time to take place on the actor.
- fixed the background colour of the combat tracker action declaration 
dropdown.

12.279
- bugfix: compendium containers now deploy items with their correct data.
- the changelog journal now links to the live changelog document.
- container notes may now be used for notes instead of for data to build the 
items contained by them.

12.278
- added a statusEffectChoice system setting that allows you to choose the 
foundry default status effects, the ones defined for the ruleset you are using 
by the system, or to define your own by creating a 'world' compendium for Items 
named 'Status Effects' and adding your Modifier items to it. They must have a 
name and an image and must be Always On because they will only be added to the 
token when the status is set and removed when it is unset. You can use either 
the token HUD to toggle your status effects or the new Token control Tool to 
'Assign Status Effects'. Click on the new tool icon to open a dialog with the 
status effects laid out in large format. Then select as many tokens as you like 
and toggle the effects you click on. Close the dialog when finished. If you 
have added modifiers to the Status Effects compendium with the same name as a 
Foundry or Ruleset Effect, your modifier item will be added and removed from 
the token as usual. Do have fun with this one.
- cleaned up the SETTINGS field in en.json and fr.json and added a few items. 
es.json is very out of date and I would be happy to work with someone to 
update it.

12.277
- added dragging death to trigger status effects thanks to Sergio. Made a 
refinement to provide basic function without extra hooks and to use the v12 
functions rather than deprecated ones.

12.276
- bugfix: creating a new actor now only creates one copy of each item, no 
matter how many GMs are logged in.
- bugfix: new items are created with the correct icon and data fields 
populated.
- bugfix: toggling the "Mark Defeated" icon for a combatant will correctly 
mark them as defeated.
- bugfix: a defeated combatant will again be marked with a red background
- feature: in the event that a token actor has been changed since it was 
placed on a scene, any rolls, including those triggered by clicking a link in 
a chat card, will refer to the actor of the selected token rather than the 
original template actor. The template actor will only be used if the token 
selected is not of that actor.

12.275
- ready for public testing and premium content is published for v12
- removed the dynamic actor sheet from the system. The bestiary has been 
upgraded with actors compatible with the classic actor sheet but you will have 
to convert / recreate any actors you have built for dynamic behaviour to 
classic behaviour. All the items and the new actor templates will likely make 
that much less painful than it might otherwise be.
- changed the Drive modifier item to use the Drive Point Bonus variable item to 
select a bonus from +0 to +50 in 10 point increments. You will have to use the 
Copy Folder Items macro to copy these items onto existing actors but all new 
actors will come with them pre-loaded.
- please let me know quickly if you spot any bugs I have missed.

