2.71
- temporary fix to the combat tracker permitting players to end their turn. The 
End Turn button will be visible to them now, even if it is not their turn so 
expect an error message if they hit the button on someone elses turn and an 
info message if they are the last combatant in a round to act, saying that they 
cannot advance the round and to inform the GM.

2.70
- added an open-ended dice modifier in the form 1d100oe. Options include 
oe2<5>96 (max depth, lower and upper targets separately), oe2=5 (max depth and 
the same range for upper and lower), oe5 (same range for upper and lower with 
no max depth), oe (default range for upper and lower of 5% of faces and no max 
depth). In all cases, the results that form an explosion are displayed as 
inactive immediately following the summarised result.
- bugfix: corrected a long-standing error in the grapple critical strikes table.

