2.14
- bugfix: found and fixed many unmigrated hyphens in the system data.
- bugfix: soul damage is applied properly again, now that Soul Damage is a 
Primary-Attribute instead of a Pool.
- NOTE: if you are having trouble with unrecognised roll types, it is likely 
that your system did not migrate properly to 2.13. Change the system setting 
for system version from 2.13 to 2.0, save and refresh. Do not touch the system 
until it says it has finished the migration. If all is not sorted by that, try 
once more, then contact me.
- improved the efficiency of data management when displaying the actor sheet.
- bugfix: Because of the fix to VsD combat, the End Turn button sometimes did 
not display for players. It now displays for them all the time.
- feature: VsD Combat now advances the round automatically when the last 
combatant ends their turn, unless it is a player, in which case the player is 
told to notify the GM to advance the round manually. Advancing the round 
manually will also reset any non-null initiatives so can act as a reset button 
or may be used to clear the current declarations.

2.13
- APECS fixes and upgrades (more to come, but this is the best version yet)
- conversion to integrated items (huge refactoring under the hood)
- migration script to help convert all references to the underscore model 
instead of hyphens.

2.12
- bugfix: At last! I think I have solved the combat tracker issue where a 
combatant who performs and interrupt not only moves to the top and looks like 
they are selected, but actually are the person who completes their turn when 
you hit end turn.

2.11
- added drag and drop behaviour for Variables and Modifiers (even between a 
Modifier and a Variable).

2.10
- bugfix: tokens will again rotate while the sheet is open.
- updated the All Items tab to a new look and function.
- am considering upgrading the entire system to the new, fully integrated item 
approach. A lot of work for no visible effect (except a performance gain) but 
then easier to maintain in common with my other systems on Foundry.
- added an updated guide to APECS in the journal compendium.

2.09
- enhanced the system settings behaviour and fixed a bug regarding the 
variable and pool placements.
- made defeated combatants a bit more obvious.
- tried to shift any APECS code out of standard VsD classes and am working on 
tidying that up incrementally.
- added the ping icon to the combat tracker. It replaces the Pings module.
- A massive overhaul of APECS, under the hood, to change it from phased to 
strictly timeline behaviour. Testing soon to see if I got it right this 
time :-)

2.08
- added the Health Adjustment macro to allow application of rolled Damage, 
Healing and Soul Damage by the GM.
- added a link to the skill description journal in skill roll chat messages.

2.07
- undid the size restriction for 2nd crit. Too many exceptions.
- added soul damage mechanic. Check the items dropbox for more stuff. You 
need to have the HP, KinVoc, Soul Damage and Soul Damage Mod from there to 
make it work. The HP that uses KinVoc for Max has been around for a while.

